OL,3,GNEWSAState pension likely to top
OL,4,A#13,000 a year as UK wage growth slows
OL,5,Ato 3.9%
OL,6,
OL,7,FThe state pension is expected to top
OL,8,F#13,000 a year, reigniting the debate
OL,9,Fabout its long-term affordability and
OL,10,Fgenerational fairness.
OL,12,FThe full, flat-rate state pension is
OL,13,Fexpected to rise by #488 a year in
OL,14,FApril, based on the latest official
OL,15,Fearnings figure released on Tuesday.
OL,17,FThe so-called triple lock pension
OL,18,Fpolicy guarantees that the state
OL,19,Fpension will increase by either average
OL,20,Fwage growth, inflation or 2.5% -
OL,21,Fwhichever is highest.
OL,23,APub: 15-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
